  "tagline": "Open-source, durable Datalog database for Clojure with Datomic-style immutable history.",
  "description": "Datahike is an open-source Datalog database for Clojure and ClojureScript that began as a durable fork of DataScript and follows Datomic's model: immutable datoms, as-of and history queries, and a pull API. Its persistent indexes are stored through the konserve abstraction, so the same database can live in memory, on files, in S3, JDBC databases or the browser, and readers can query directly from storage. It is the main open-source alternative for teams who like Datomic's model but want source access, embedded use or ClojureScript support. Throughput and tooling are modest, and the ecosystem is almost entirely Clojure.",
